      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(markdown-core): break multi-line frontmatter value on empty lines",
        "body": "fix(markdown-core): break multi-line frontmatter value on empty lines\n\n## Description\n\nIn `parseSimpleFrontmatterValues`, the condition `(line && !/^[ \\t]/.test(line))` uses a truthy-check on `line`. An empty line (`\"\"`) is falsy, so it bypasses the break and is incorrectly consumed as a continuation of the multi-line value. This causes blank lines between indented continuation lines to be included in the parsed value instead of terminating it.\n\n## Fix\n\nRemoved the `line &&` guard. An empty line now correctly exits the continuation loop since `!/^[ \\t]/.test(\"\")` is `true`.\n\n## Real module test evidence (vitest, 24/24 passed)\n\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  24 passed (24)\n```\n\n```\n ✓ parses YAML block scalars\n ✓ handles JSON5-style multi-line metadata\n ✓ preserves inline JSON values\n ✓ normalizes free-form descriptions before YAML parsing\n ✓ parses frontmatter after a leading UTF-8 BOM\n ✓ ... (24 total)\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/frontmatter-empty-line-break",
